// =====================================================================
// SCENE 2 · GAP 1: THE NOTES (00:00)
// Midnight, empty school. In a "dream", Anin reads Fal's locker and
// learns he is the only child who must be "great". She writes notes and
// hides them in his math textbook. In the dream the words blur as she
// writes: the player NEVER sees what the notes say in this scene.
//
// NOTES FOR THE PROGRAMMER
// - Every "//" comment is a stage direction for you, not in-game text.
// - WRITING RULE: every line night Anin says is true. She withholds,
//   she never lies. Please don't add lines without checking with N.
// - Commands used (rename to match your Dialogue Runner):
//     <<gap_mode true/false>>         gap visuals: colour grade, near
//                                     silence, all clocks frozen at 00:00
//     <<quest_start "id" "Title">>    start / show a quest
//     <<quest_update "id" "Title">>   update the quest objective
//     <<scene_transition "Location">> fade + load a location
//     <<give_item "id">>              add item to inventory
//     <<remove_item "id">>            remove item from inventory
//     <<open_locker "id">>            locker open animation
//     <<close_locker "id">>           locker close animation
//     <<blur_writing "id">>           writing animation: pen moves, the
//                                     words smear and stay unreadable
//     <<end_gap>>                     second hand moves, fade to Dec 10
// - <<scene_transition>> loads the room and ends the node there. A <<jump X>> after
//   it never runs: node X must be the start node (YarnCutscene) of that room instead.
// - NO NPCs exist in the gap. Kirana's bed is empty, blanket flat.
// - The ROOFTOP key IS on its hook in this scene (it was empty in Scene 1).
// - The notes' real text is cruel (e.g. "You are not good enough",
//   "You're a disgrace to your family"). It is ONLY revealed in Scene 5
//   (Day 3 midpoint), as a flashback in Anin's handwriting. Do not show
//   it anywhere in this scene, including UI, item names or tooltips.
// =====================================================================


// ---------------------------------------------------------------------
// DORM — 00:00
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------

title: Gap1_Start
tags: scene2 gap1 dorm
---
<<gap_mode true>>
// Lets the Dorm door run Gap1_Dorm_Door instead of leaving freely.
<<set $story_exit to true>>
<<set $gap1_master_key to false>>
<<set $gap1_locker_open to false>>
<<set $gap1_seen_photo to false>>
<<set $gap1_seen_report to false>>
<<set $gap1_seen_letter to false>>
<<set $gap1_seen_rocket to false>>
<<set $gap1_seen_note to false>>
<<set $gap1_notes_placed to false>>
<<set $gap1_locker_closed to false>>
<<set $gap1_key_returned to false>>

// Anin opens her eyes. The room is wrong: too quiet, too still.
// Kirana's bed is empty, the blanket flat as if no one was ever there.
// Double reading: first play = tired deja vu. Replay = night Anin's
// weary "again", the same word she ends Chapter 1 on (Scene 8).
Anin: ...Again.
<<quest_start "gap1" "Something's wrong with Fal">>
// Interactables: Gap1_Dorm_Clock, Gap1_Dorm_KiranaBed,
// Gap1_Dorm_Window, Gap1_Dorm_Door
===

title: Gap1_Dorm_Clock
tags: scene2 gap1 dorm interactable
---
Anin: Midnight. It's not moving.
===

title: Gap1_Dorm_KiranaBed
tags: scene2 gap1 dorm interactable
---
Anin: Gone again.
===

title: Gap1_Dorm_Window
tags: scene2 gap1 dorm interactable
---
Anin: The whole school is dark. Like it's holding its breath.
===

title: Gap1_Dorm_Door
tags: scene2 gap1 dorm interactable
---
<<if $gap1_key_returned is false>>
    // First visit: leaving for the school.
    // Double reading: the player hears "end his death"; on replay, "end the loop".
    Anin: If I understand him, I can end this.
    <<quest_update "gap1" "Find out why">>
    <<scene_transition "LockerRoom">>
    <<jump Gap1_Lockers_Start>>
<<else>>
    Anin: I should sleep.
<<endif>>
===


// ---------------------------------------------------------------------
// LOCKER ROOM — 00:00
// Same room where she waited in Scene 1. Moonlight through the high
// window. Her footsteps are the only sound.
// Interactables: Gap1_KeyHook, Gap1_JanitorCabinet, Gap1_FalLocker
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------

title: Gap1_Lockers_Start
tags: scene2 gap1 lockers
---
// Both Locker Room exits play their Story Nodes instead of leaving during this scene.
<<set $story_exit to true>>
// No dialogue on entry. Let the silence play.
===

title: Gap1_Lockers_DormExit
tags: scene2 gap1 lockers interactable
---
Anin: I can't go back now.
===

title: Gap1_Lockers_MapExit
tags: scene2 gap1 lockers interactable
---
Anin: No use wandering around
===

title: Gap1_KeyHook
tags: scene2 gap1 lockers interactable
---
// Hook tag: ROOFTOP. The key is back on the hook.
Anin: Back on its hook. Like nothing happened.
===

title: Gap1_JanitorCabinet
tags: scene2 gap1 lockers interactable
---
<<if $gap1_master_key is false and $gap1_key_returned is false>>
    <<sfx "janitor_cabinet_open">>
    Anin: The master key. Sorry, Pak.
    <<give_item "master_key">>
    <<set $gap1_master_key to true>>
<<elseif $gap1_master_key is true and $gap1_locker_closed is true>>
    <<jump Gap1_ReturnKey>>
<<else>>
    Anin: I still need it.
<<endif>>
===

title: Gap1_FalLocker
tags: scene2 gap1 lockers interactable
---
// Fal's locker, rocket sticker on the door.
<<if $gap1_master_key is false>>
    <<sfx "ui_error">>
    Anin: Locked.
<<elseif $gap1_notes_placed is true>>
    // Checked before $gap1_locker_open, so closing it never opens it again.
    Anin: Close it. Put the key back. Like I was never here.
    <<if $gap1_locker_closed is false>>
        <<close_locker "fal">>
        // Hides the locker contents (ActiveIfYarnVariable with Follow Changes).
        <<set $gap1_locker_open to false>>
        <<set $gap1_locker_closed to true>>
        <<quest_update "gap1" "Return the master key">>
    <<endif>>
<<elseif $gap1_locker_open is false>>
    Anin: I'm sorry, Fal. I need to know.
    <<open_locker "fal">>
    // Shows the locker contents (ActiveIfYarnVariable with Follow Changes).
    <<set $gap1_locker_open to true>>
    <<quest_update "gap1" "Look through Fal's locker">>
    <<jump Gap1_LockerContents>>
<<endif>>
===


// ---------------------------------------------------------------------
// LOCKER CONTENTS — dialogue options, all five must be chosen before
// writing the notes. Each item node jumps back to the menu; a chosen
// option is hidden (Options Presenter: Show Unavailable Options off).
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------

title: Gap1_LockerContents
tags: scene2 gap1 lockers
---
<<if $gap1_seen_photo and $gap1_seen_report and $gap1_seen_letter and $gap1_seen_rocket and $gap1_seen_note>>
    <<jump Gap1_CheckContents>>
<<endif>>
-> The photo <<if $gap1_seen_photo is false>>
    <<jump Gap1_Photo>>
-> The report card <<if $gap1_seen_report is false>>
    <<jump Gap1_ReportCard>>
-> The letter <<if $gap1_seen_letter is false>>
    <<jump Gap1_Letter>>
-> Something folded <<if $gap1_seen_rocket is false>>
    <<jump Gap1_Rocket>>
-> The sealed note <<if $gap1_seen_note is false>>
    <<jump Gap1_SealedNote>>
===

title: Gap1_Photo
tags: scene2 gap1 lockers
---
<<sfx "paper_handle">>
// Text only for now, no close-up art.
Anin: A family photo. Fal and his parents, in front of a hospital.
Anin: They're all smiling. Except his eyes.
Anin: Just the three of them. He's all they've got.
<<set $gap1_seen_photo to true>>
<<jump Gap1_LockerContents>>
===

title: Gap1_ReportCard
tags: scene2 gap1 lockers
---
<<sfx "paper_handle">>
// Text only for now, no close-up art.
Anin: His report card. Math, sixty-one. Class rank, seven.
Anin: Someone wrote on it in red pen. "Not enough."
Anin: That's his dad's writing.
<<set $gap1_seen_report to true>>
<<jump Gap1_LockerContents>>
===

title: Gap1_Letter
tags: scene2 gap1 lockers
---
<<sfx "paper_handle">>
// Text only for now, no close-up art. Sets up the pressure Fal is under.
Anin: A letter from home.
Anin: "Fal, we've given everything so you can be great. Top three. Medicine. Don't waste it. Don't let us down."
Anin: "Don't let us down."
<<set $gap1_seen_letter to true>>
<<jump Gap1_LockerContents>>
===

title: Gap1_Rocket
tags: scene2 gap1 lockers
---
<<sfx "paper_handle">>
// Text only for now, no close-up art.
Anin: Something folded small, tucked behind the letter.
Anin: A rocket. He drew it so carefully.
Anin: In the corner, in his handwriting: "someday?"
Anin: He never told anyone he wanted this.
<<set $gap1_seen_rocket to true>>
<<jump Gap1_LockerContents>>
===

title: Gap1_SealedNote
tags: scene2 gap1 lockers
---
<<sfx "paper_handle">>
// Text only for now, no close-up art.
// It must NOT be openable in this scene.
Anin: A folded note. My name on the front, in his handwriting.
Anin: It's still sealed.
Anin: ...Not mine to read. Not yet.
<<set $gap1_seen_note to true>>
<<jump Gap1_LockerContents>>
===

title: Gap1_CheckContents
tags: scene2 gap1 lockers
---
Anin: He's carrying all of this alone. Someone has to say something to him.
<<jump Gap1_WriteNotes>>
===


// ---------------------------------------------------------------------
// WRITING THE NOTES
// No choices. The player watches the pen move but the words blur, like
// trying to read in a dream. Night Anin's lines stay true: she never
// says the words are kind. The player fills that in.
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------

title: Gap1_WriteNotes
tags: scene2 gap1 lockers
---
<<quest_update "gap1" "Write something for Fal">>
Anin: Something he'll read when he needs it most.
<<blur_writing "notes_for_fal">>
Anin: No name. It'll mean more that way.
<<jump Gap1_MathBook>>
===


// ---------------------------------------------------------------------
// PLACING THE NOTES
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------

title: Gap1_MathBook
tags: scene2 gap1 lockers
---
// Fal's math textbook, the one he brought for tutoring.
Anin: He'll open this tomorrow. For our session.
// Show the notes being slipped between the pages.
<<sfx "paper_placement">>
<<set $gap1_notes_placed to true>>
// Double reading: "it" = saving him (first play) / the plan (replay).
Anin: He has to read these. This time it'll work.
<<quest_update "gap1" "Close the locker">>
// Next interactable: Gap1_FalLocker (closes the locker)
===


// ---------------------------------------------------------------------
// RETURNING THE MASTER KEY (required before leaving)
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------

title: Gap1_ReturnKey
tags: scene2 gap1 lockers
---
<<remove_item "master_key">>
<<set $gap1_master_key to false>>
<<set $gap1_key_returned to true>>
<<quest_update "gap1" "Go back to bed">>
<<scene_transition "Dorm">>
<<jump Gap1_Dorm_End>>
===


// ---------------------------------------------------------------------
// DORM — 00:00 (END)
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------

title: Gap1_Dorm_End
tags: scene2 gap1 dorm
---
// Anin lies down. The clock still reads 00:00.
<<sfx "bed_drop">>
Anin: Please. Let this be the last time.
// The second hand moves.
<<gap_mode false>>
<<set $chapter_scene to 3>>
<<end_gap>>
// TRANSITION → Scene 3: Day 2 (Dec 10 morning)
===
